WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:09.090 --> 00:00:13.840
If someone is in the hospital and
they're really sick, there's really

00:00:13.840 --> 00:00:17.590
nothing that a clinician can do other
than give them supportive care.

00:00:17.590 --> 00:00:23.529
What we've been trying to do is develop
broad-spectrum antivirals that work

00:00:23.529 --> 00:00:28.000
not only against the coronaviruses that
we know about today like SARS-CoV-2, the

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:33.370
causative agent of COVID-19, but also we
want these things to have a broad

00:00:33.370 --> 00:00:37.900
application against coronaviruses that
might emerge in the future.

00:00:40.140 --> 00:00:43.320
A vaccine basically is something that you take as a preventative measure.

00:00:43.320 --> 00:00:45.040
So this could be COVID-19 a vaccine against

00:00:45.080 --> 00:00:46.940
SARS-coronavirus-2, SARS-CoV-2,

00:00:46.940 --> 00:00:49.300
the causative agent of COVID-19.

00:00:49.300 --> 00:00:53.100
If we got a vaccine then we
would be our bodies would be protected

00:00:53.109 --> 00:00:58.329
from infection by that agent. So what an
antiviral drug does, it's different:

00:00:58.329 --> 00:01:03.309
most of the time you're taking these things
after you know you got sick to try and

00:01:03.309 --> 00:01:07.120
decrease the symptoms that you might
have and prevent the development of

00:01:07.120 --> 00:01:12.250
severe disease. And you might prevent
lots of older people or people that have

00:01:12.250 --> 00:01:14.920
underlying health conditions from going
to the hospital

00:01:14.960 --> 00:01:18.520
and ending up on a ventilator.

00:01:19.900 --> 00:01:24.260
We started working on Remdesivir five or six years ago.

00:01:24.260 --> 00:01:29.420
All of that work set this drug up for immediate deployment into human

00:01:29.420 --> 00:01:34.080
clinical trials for COVID-19. I think
that's different than like someone who

00:01:34.090 --> 00:01:38.049
might find something today. Right? They
have to do all the work that we've been

00:01:38.049 --> 00:01:42.540
doing for the past five years before
they can use this drug in a person

00:01:42.560 --> 00:01:45.440
or even test it for safety.

00:01:47.540 --> 00:01:52.580
There are several human clinical trials
all over the world evaluating the

00:01:52.580 --> 00:01:57.560
potential for different antiviral drugs
to have some effect on COVID-19:

00:01:57.560 --> 00:02:02.940
Remdesivir, chloroquine, some of the HIV
protease inhibitors, and some of these

00:02:02.960 --> 00:02:06.680
other things. We can basically close the
door or open the door on these things

00:02:06.680 --> 00:02:10.320
and say this is useful... this is hurtful.

00:02:10.640 --> 00:02:13.620
It's hard to know which way the wind is gonna blow

